A||||17||ChadMan||IMSA Fiero info and pix from Mid-Ohio||||1
Z||000000||ChadMan||10-11-1999||01:35 PM||||Two guys (John Kerkhoff and Mike Varat) from CA raced last weekend in the GT2 class at the SCCA Nationals with an IMSA GTU Fiero.  I spoke at length with Mike about the car and took several photos, seven of which I have scanned as JPEGs.  John raced the car on Friday, started dead last (22nd), but finshed 15th.<P>Could someone please give me DETAILED instructions on how to post these pix on the Forum?  I don't have my own web site (yet).<P>Mike told me a great deal about this car.  It was originally built by Joe Huffaker and raced as #75, sponsored by the Pontiac Fiero Assembly Plant workers.  It is powered by a 2.7 liter Super Duty 4-banger making approx 275 hp.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||10-11-1999||03:16 PM||||Chadman, just click on the "Pennock's Image Poster" button on the bottom of this (and every other) page and you'll find detailed instructions how to post images here. I'm <B>very</B> curious about this IMSA Fiero, the only one I've seen so far was a 5" R/C!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||10-11-1999||04:35 PM||||I downloaded PIP, but I'm out of time for today.  I will try to post these images tomorrow.  Stay tuned...||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||10-12-1999||08:51 AM||||OK, I used PIP, and it told me I have successfully uploaded 7 images.  Time to press Ctrl-V and see what happens... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IMSAfiero7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
