Z||000012||Cliff Pennock||10-12-1999||03:11 PM||||PS ChadMan, I noticed that you posted every image (except the first) double. You don't need to repost an image to include it in a message with CTL-V. Just click on the "History" button, there you'll see all the images you have posted (and you'll notice that you have posted most images twice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). If you click on the button with the image's name, you can then use it in a message again by pressing CTL-V (without posting it again!).||||reg||4
Z||000013||ChadMan||10-12-1999||05:18 PM||||Sorry to waste your server space, Cliff.  The Pennock Image Poster is great!<P>More IMSA Fiero facts...<P>According to Mike Varat, only 13 of these cars were built.<BR>The car uses a 4-speed transmission with the stock 1984 transaxle case containing "racing gears."<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000014||lowCG||10-12-1999||09:23 PM||||Slurp drool,uh,oh yeah,would love to see that car in action,must sound really nice with those Webers.<BR>Cliff,I think those wheels are Compomotives,from England,I had a set on a Lancia Montecarlo,they're pretty heavy,three separate castings;what you'd want if you were going 200mph,but would slow you down really for the power our cars make.<BR>Wonder how light that car is?||||reg||1
Z||000015||ChadMan||10-13-1999||08:09 AM||||Car and Driver listed a curb weight for the IMSA GTU Fiero of 2050 lbs.  I didn't think to ask Mike if theirs was running at the same weight in SCCA GT-2.  D'oh!||||reg||1
